# Cursor Rules — OvO Portfolio

## Context
This is a developer portfolio site (Korean/English toggle) built with Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, PostgreSQL (Neon), Prisma.
Owner: 오리 — Ewha Womans University, Computer Engineering, graduating Feb 2027.

**Always read `SPEC.md` and `CLAUDE.md` before significant changes.**

## Current Phase
Phase 1: Static version with dummy data. Design system + main page only.
**Do NOT implement** modals, DB, auth, image upload, markdown rendering, drag-drop, filters.

## Design Tokens (strict)
- Color base: monochrome (black / white / gray)
- Accent: slate blue (`#4a6fa5` light, `#6b8cc4` dark) — use CSS variables
- No arbitrary Tailwind colors. Use semantic tokens only.
- Fonts: Pretendard (KR) + Inter (EN) for sans, Geist Mono for mono
- Container max-width 1100px
- Border radius: 8px cards, 6px buttons/tags, 999px chips/avatar

## Conventions
- Functional components, named exports
- kebab-case filenames, PascalCase component names
- Use `cn()` helper for class composition
- No `any` — use `unknown` if truly unknown
- All user-facing text via `next-intl` messages
- Minimize `"use client"` — prefer Server Components
- Every interactive element: aria-label, visible focus state

## File Structure
```
src/
  app/[locale]/
  components/sections/
  components/ui/
  lib/
  data/
  i18n/
  messages/
  types/
```

## Style Tone Reference
Linear + Vercel + Rauno + Brittany Chiang blended.
Restrained color, generous whitespace, sharp typography hierarchy.

## What Cursor should NOT do
- Add libraries without checking SPEC.md
- Hardcode Korean/English strings
- Use arbitrary Tailwind colors (e.g. `bg-blue-500`)
- Implement features outside Phase 1 scope
- Add `console.log` in committed code
- Skip TypeScript types